  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">SHRIMP AQUACULTURE CONTAMINANTS &amp; SHOREBIRDS - NE BRAZIL</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">This project seeks to increase understanding of contaminant exposure that shorebirds may experience at commercial shrimp farms during migration and wintering periods in northeastern Brazil, leading to the development of best management practices that reduce exposure. Ultimately, this will lead to solutions that incorporate shorebird conservation needs into shrimp aquaculture permitting processes, promote sustainable shrimp aquaculture development and alleviate competition between conservation and economic priorities. Birds that will benefit include red knot, semipalmated sandpiper, lesser and greater yellowlegs, short-billed dowitcher, ruddy turnstone, black-bellied plover, willet, and whimbrel...</narrative>
  </description>
